xnu: 0184 proc_exit skip early proc_prepareexit (EXIT_PROBE A->B deadlock)

EXIT_PROBE A_entry fires for fsck(pid 2) but B_post_terminate never does:
the boot-task wedges inside the first-entry branch of proc_exit, i.e.
proc_prepareexit(p, 0, TRUE) or task_terminate_internal. Disable the
prepareexit call first (Jetsam path suspicion: repeated 'Could not opt
into 50 MB Jetsam high watermark' errors at launchd init).
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
@@ -2108,7 +2108,9 @@
 		p->p_lflag |= P_LEXIT;
 		proc_transend(p, 1);
 		proc_unlock(p);
-		proc_prepareexit(p, 0, TRUE);
+	/* VINCE: skipped - EXIT_PROBE A_entry fires but B_post_terminate never does;
+	   deadlock sits in proc_prepareexit (Jetsam/cleanup) on boot-task exit. */
+	if (0) proc_prepareexit(p, 0, TRUE);
 		(void) task_terminate_internal(task);
 		proc_lock(p);
 	} else if (!(p->p_lflag & P_LTERM)) {
